WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.230
- So, we lost Queen Elizabeth
this year and not long ago,

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.100
I wanna get this right,

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.360
she made you an officer

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.870
of the most excellent order
of the British Empire.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.600
(audience cheering)

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.800
- That's a lot of words.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.350
- I feel like, it's very fancy

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.200
and I just wanna know what it means.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.200
- Very good question.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.337
I'm not sure I can entirely
tell you what it means.

00:00:21.337 --> 00:00:22.532
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:22.532 --> 00:00:25.260
It was an extraordinary moment.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.150
You you get a medal.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:27.983
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:27.983 --> 00:00:29.892
- And you line up in Windsor Castle,

00:00:29.892 --> 00:00:33.453
alongside these people who've done really

00:00:33.453 --> 00:00:35.507
brilliant things like, you know,

00:00:35.507 --> 00:00:38.820
people in charge of the health service,

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:43.230
or who've sort of curing cancer.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.980
And you are the person who
like, you know, play the part.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:47.580
So you feel sort of pretty outta all.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.520
But also you get a lesson
in how to genuflect

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:51.870
and how to kind of what to say

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:54.000
and when to move forward.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.890
And when we were being told this,

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.500
it just for me, went in
one ear and out the other.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:03.500
And I went in to meet the
queen and everything went out.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.946
And I just sort of mumbled
and kept doing that basically.

00:01:06.946 --> 00:01:09.630
But it was a very, very special moment.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.497
- I just love that you
can say that sentence,

00:01:11.497 --> 00:01:13.225
"When I walked in to meet the queen."

00:01:13.225 --> 00:01:15.510
It's just like a really cool
sentence to be able to say.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.310
- But we have these odd things in it.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.377
There was another thing
that I got which was called,

00:01:20.377 --> 00:01:22.290
"The Freedom of the City of London."

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:25.395
And it's a very beautiful
sort of certificate you get

00:01:25.395 --> 00:01:27.427
and you go to a meet, I was
offered in and I was like,

00:01:27.427 --> 00:01:28.260
"God, how wonderful."

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:29.093
It's very historical.

00:01:29.093 --> 00:01:31.350
I can't tell you exactly what it is.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:32.733
But when I went to the ceremony,

00:01:32.733 --> 00:01:35.774
they said, "And what you get for this

00:01:35.774 --> 00:01:38.730
is you are now legally allowed

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:42.364
to lead sheep across London Bridge."

00:01:42.364 --> 00:01:44.959
(audience cheering)

00:01:44.959 --> 00:01:48.690
And I get to lead sheep
across London Bridge.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:50.880
- This is a really old award.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.383
This has to be very old award.

00:01:53.383 --> 00:01:54.960
Do you own sheep?

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.600
- I don't own own sheep.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.677
- You should get some, just
to walk it across and be like,

00:01:59.677 --> 00:02:00.750
"I can do this, and you can't."

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.370
- Can you imagine?

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:05.010
I mean I have felt like I
want to put that to test.

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:07.920
I think if I really sort
of took some sheep on leads

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.514
across London Bridge, I might
get stopped by the police.

00:02:10.514 --> 00:02:12.813
- Who cares? Just show your certificate.

00:02:12.813 --> 00:02:15.540
- Brandishing my certificate.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:16.620
- Yeah. Just hold it.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:19.770
Have it like hanging
like the spelling bee.

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:20.610
- Redmans' lost it.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:21.703
He's totally lost the plot.

00:02:21.703 --> 00:02:23.040
- I just think that's amazing

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.150
'cause it's such an old thing

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:25.710
that probably was a huge deal back then

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:26.550
that you could actually.

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:27.383
- Take the sheep across.

00:02:27.383 --> 00:02:28.216
- Take the sheep.

00:02:28.216 --> 00:02:29.790
Well, because that is for farmers.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:30.623
That's good.

00:02:30.623 --> 00:02:31.650
You get like different
grass over there, whatever.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.060
That's probably a really great thing.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:33.893
- A massive deal, yeah.

00:02:33.893 --> 00:02:34.980
- Not so much now.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:35.813
- Well, I mean.

00:02:35.813 --> 00:02:37.350
- [Kelly] Until you try it.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:38.200
- Until I try it.

